[{"id":3498038803,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Qf9YT","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19a2a4ff85&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","login":"KoBeWi","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi"},"body":"I wonder about the performance implications, especially making `get_top_selected_node_list()` return a new list.\n\nAnd speaking of `top_selected_node_list`, does it have to still be a list? It could be LocalVector, since it's no longer returned directly. Although the way this list is used, I wonder if it needs to be changed at all. You are copying ObjectIDs into it, but then it's only ever returned and not used in any other way. But I guess making it still use pointers can create some unsafe edge case.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111837#pullrequestreview-3498038803","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111837","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-11-24T13:05:47Z"},{"id":3592848198,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7WJoNG","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"338cfba60a7cc9ea0f98f50f7775342e392ce4c0","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19a2a4ff85&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","login":"KoBeWi","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengi